  "problem": "Express $1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218})$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061{15}^{\u2218} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot {15}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
